<p>The sundial on the garden front of Wilanów Palace, around 1684, on the south-eastern corner pavilion. Not one dial but three: equal hours in the centre, Italian hours on the left counted from the last sunset, Babylonian hours on the right counted from sunrise.</p>
{% include "przyrzady/gnomon.njk" %}
<p class="note">At Wilanów the sundial and the mechanical clock never show the same hour. The gap is made of the equation of time plus a fixed correction of six degrees east of the zone meridian.</p>
<p class="note uwaga">The model assumes a wall facing due south and a gnomon perpendicular to it.</p>
